From d920ea0e5ee940f1e91dc0ac8a736dd94caa0ac1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Mar 2026 03:42:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(keymap): include reserved layers in stock layer ordering
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

load_stock_keymap_layer_ordering() used DT_INST_FOREACH_CHILD_STATUS_OKAY
to populate keymap_layer_orders[], which skips DTS nodes with
status = "reserved". This left those slots as ZMK_KEYMAP_LAYER_ID_INVAL,
making any layer placed after a reserved node unreachable in the key
dispatch loop in zmk_keymap_position_state_changed().

The binding stored in &mo/&lt/&lt_b correctly passes the DTS child index
as the layer ID, and ZMK_KEYMAP_LAYERS_LEN is counted via
DT_FOREACH_CHILD (all children). The mismatch was only in this ordering
table: STATUS_OKAY skipped reserved nodes, so layer IDs beyond the last
reserved node never appeared in keymap_layer_orders[] and could never be
activated.

Fix by using DT_INST_FOREACH_CHILD instead, so all DTS children—including
reserved ones—are assigned consecutive IDs in the ordering table. Reserved
layers have zero-initialized bindings and are transparent in dispatch.
---
 app/src/keymap.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/app/src/keymap.c b/app/src/keymap.c
index 547d661..75c1c2d 100644
--- a/app/src/keymap.c
+++ b/app/src/keymap.c
@@ -595,7 +595,7 @@ int zmk_keymap_save_changes(void) {
 
 static void load_stock_keymap_layer_ordering() {
     int i = 0;
-    DT_INST_FOREACH_CHILD_STATUS_OKAY(0, KEYMAP_LAYER_ORDER_INIT)
+    DT_INST_FOREACH_CHILD(0, KEYMAP_LAYER_ORDER_INIT)
     while (i < ZMK_KEYMAP_LAYERS_LEN) {
         keymap_layer_orders[i] = ZMK_KEYMAP_LAYER_ID_INVAL;
         i++;
-- 
